  "question": {
    "text": "Six molecules of an ideal gas have velocities \\(1,3,5,5,6\\) and \\(5 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}\\) respectively. At any given temperature, if \\(\\overline{V}\\) and \\(V_{\\mathrm{rms}}\\) represent average and rms speed of the molecules, then",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "Iwaz7",
      "text": "\\(\\overline{V}=5 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "WCdFY",
      "text": "\\(V_{r m s} > \\overline{V}\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "LNxjc",
      "text": "\\(V_{\\text {rms }}^2  < \\overline{V}^2\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "rFZpt",
      "text": "\\(V_{r m s}=\\overline{V}\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hint : \\(\\overline{V}=\\frac{1+3+5+5+6+5}{6}=\\frac{25}{6}=4.16\\)\n\\(\\begin{aligned}\n& \\overline{V}_{\\mathrm{ms}}=\\sqrt{\\frac{1+9+25 \\times 3+36}{6}}=\\sqrt{\\frac{121}{6}}=\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{6}}=4.48 \\\\\n& \\mathrm{~V}_{\\mathrm{rms}} > \\overline{V}\n\\end{aligned}\\)",
    "image": null
